1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,538
Welcome to this technical walkthrough of AI-Based Predictive
Maintenance for Mining Equipment.

2
00:00:05,758 --> 00:00:11,548
The project team is Ganesh Mishra, Lakshya Sharma and Sagar
Patel, from

3
00:00:11,548 --> 00:00:15,890
Saskatchewan Polytechnic, under the guidance of Doctor Himanshu
Patel.

4
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:22,834
This video explains the objectives, data sources, software
design, code and actual

5
00:00:22,834 --> 00:00:23,954
prediction outputs.

6
00:00:24,174 --> 00:00:28,305
The narration is computer generated; it is not a recording of a

7
00:00:28,305 --> 00:00:29,338
team member speaking.

8
00:00:29,558 --> 00:00:34,388
The execution examples were run against the existing local
checkpoints and are

9
00:00:34,388 --> 00:00:35,998
replayed here for readability.

10
00:00:36,218 --> 00:00:40,336
The implemented task is current component fault classification.

11
00:00:40,556 --> 00:00:45,138
Although predictive maintenance is the project title, the
software does not estimate

12
00:00:45,138 --> 00:00:47,430
the date of a future failure.

13
00:00:47,650 --> 00:00:51,291
That distinction will remain visible throughout the
demonstration.

14
00:00:51,511 --> 00:00:57,005
Mining operations depend on components such as bearings, motors
and geared drives.

15
00:00:57,225 --> 00:01:00,993
A fault in one component may interrupt the larger process.

16
00:01:01,213 --> 00:01:08,123
The project asks whether available condition-monitoring
measurements can support a practical fault-classification

17
00:01:08,123 --> 00:01:08,698
prototype.

18
00:01:08,918 --> 00:01:14,743
The software objective is straightforward: accept a supported
file, apply the correct

19
00:01:14,743 --> 00:01:19,597
preprocessing, load an existing model, and display its predicted
condition.

20
00:01:19,817 --> 00:01:24,932
The research objective is harder: compare sensor and visual
evidence using fault

21
00:01:24,932 --> 00:01:30,048
targets that are mechanically comparable, and test how results
change under proper

22
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:30,901
group separation.

23
00:01:31,121 --> 00:01:36,004
A working upload button alone cannot establish that a classifier
generalizes.

24
00:01:36,224 --> 00:01:42,164
For that reason, the project keeps software execution checks
separate from held-out

25
00:01:42,164 --> 00:01:43,154
experimental performance.

26
00:01:43,374 --> 00:01:46,905
Both are necessary, but they answer different questions.

27
00:01:47,125 --> 00:01:52,764
The research background combines conventional condition
monitoring with visual transfer learning.

28
00:01:52,984 --> 00:01:59,347
Sensor measurements can be summarized using statistical and
spectral features, making tree

29
00:01:59,347 --> 00:02:04,119
ensembles, support vector machines and logistic regression
useful candidates.

30
00:02:04,339 --> 00:02:09,302
Random forests provide a practical baseline for mixed numerical
features.

31
00:02:09,522 --> 00:02:15,836
For visual inputs, the project uses ImageNet-pretrained ResNet18
representations.

32
00:02:16,056 --> 00:02:21,499
Most visual routes fine tune a classifier, while the gear-tooth
photograph route

33
00:02:21,499 --> 00:02:24,220
uses frozen features with logistic regression.

34
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:28,337
These algorithm choices do not remove weaknesses in the data.

35
00:02:28,557 --> 00:02:33,348
A model may learn a recording, operating speed or camera setup
instead

36
00:02:33,348 --> 00:02:35,344
of a transferable fault signature.

37
00:02:35,564 --> 00:02:40,405
The central methodological choice is therefore the way training
and testing are

38
00:02:40,405 --> 00:02:40,808
separated.

39
00:02:41,028 --> 00:02:45,950
Dataset sources and the original model references are documented
in the final

40
00:02:45,950 --> 00:02:46,360
report.

41
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:53,080
The system contains eight mining-equipment application mappings:
Pump, Haul Truck, Belt Conveyor,

42
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:57,955
Dozer, Excavator, Wheel Loader, Drill Rig and Motor Grader.

43
00:02:58,175 --> 00:03:02,653
These names describe intended applications of laboratory
components.

44
00:03:02,873 --> 00:03:06,770
They do not mean that every dataset was collected from the named

45
00:03:06,770 --> 00:03:07,420
mining machine.

46
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:10,747
Pump and Haul Truck use bearing-related evidence.

47
00:03:10,967 --> 00:03:16,652
Conveyor and Dozer use geared-drive evidence, with Dozer reusing
the conveyor benchmark.

48
00:03:16,872 --> 00:03:20,977
Excavator and Wheel Loader use related drive and motor tasks.

49
00:03:21,197 --> 00:03:26,480
Drill Rig uses gearbox data, while the aligned Motor Grader
comparison concerns

50
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:27,360
gear damage.

51
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:31,874
The original Motor Grader bearing route is also preserved as a
separate

52
00:03:31,874 --> 00:03:32,232
task.

53
00:03:32,452 --> 00:03:37,262
Reuse of the same rig or records is explicitly disclosed, so
eight

54
00:03:37,262 --> 00:03:41,270
application rows are not presented as eight independent field
trials.

55
00:03:41,490 --> 00:03:47,938
The sensor sources include Ottawa and UODS bearing measurements,
CORA electromechanical measurements,

56
00:03:47,938 --> 00:03:54,386
MCC5 gearbox vibration, Aalto gear measurements and the separate
JUST bearing task.

57
00:03:54,606 --> 00:04:01,759
Visual sources include XJTU dynamic-vision recordings, CORA
infrared frames, synthetic MFGNet gear

58
00:04:01,759 --> 00:04:05,336
renders and real GearBox tooth photographs.

59
00:04:05,556 --> 00:04:09,382
Event-camera frames are not ordinary colour photographs.

60
00:04:09,602 --> 00:04:14,107
Synthetic renders are not camera measurements from damaged
mining equipment.

61
00:04:14,327 --> 00:04:18,820
Multiple frames, windows or tooth crops may come from one source
group,

62
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:23,312
so their count must not be confused with a count of independent

63
00:04:23,312 --> 00:04:23,687
machines.

64
00:04:23,907 --> 00:04:28,884
The dataset manifest records the source mappings and available
local files.

65
00:04:29,104 --> 00:04:34,039
Raw data and large checkpoints stay outside the public code
archive, and

66
00:04:34,039 --> 00:04:37,329
the local installation needs access to those prerequisites.

67
00:04:37,549 --> 00:04:42,079
The block diagram begins with a file supplied through the
notebook, command

68
00:04:42,079 --> 00:04:43,967
line or local upload page.

69
00:04:44,187 --> 00:04:48,674
The system validates the input and tries to identify a known
source

70
00:04:48,674 --> 00:04:49,048
format.

71
00:04:49,268 --> 00:04:53,835
If the source is compatible with more than one equipment
mapping, it

72
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:56,880
returns an ambiguity warning rather than silently guessing.

73
00:04:57,100 --> 00:05:01,611
A sensor file is converted into the features expected by its
checkpoint.

74
00:05:01,831 --> 00:05:05,054
An image is transformed according to the visual route.

75
00:05:05,274 --> 00:05:10,814
The saved model produces class probabilities, and the largest
output determines the

76
00:05:10,814 --> 00:05:11,737
displayed condition.

77
00:05:11,957 --> 00:05:17,156
Both modalities share the same prediction entry point, but they
remain independent

78
00:05:17,156 --> 00:05:17,589
models.

79
00:05:17,809 --> 00:05:21,532
There is no fusion of unrelated sensor and image samples.

80
00:05:21,752 --> 00:05:27,522
The final output includes the application mapping, fault label,
model probability and

81
00:05:27,522 --> 00:05:28,483
model used.

82
00:05:28,703 --> 00:05:33,286
The submitted notebook is the main explanation and demonstration
entry point.

83
00:05:33,506 --> 00:05:39,336
Its first code cell imports the standard libraries, numerical
packages, plotting tools

84
00:05:39,336 --> 00:05:40,793
and upload widgets.

85
00:05:41,013 --> 00:05:46,314
It locates the project folder and imports predictive maintenance
as the application

86
00:05:46,314 --> 00:05:46,756
module.

87
00:05:46,976 --> 00:05:51,450
The implementation is kept in that companion Python file so the
notebook

88
00:05:51,450 --> 00:05:55,552
does not duplicate thousands of lines of model and interface
logic.

89
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:59,217
The notebook and companion code must be submitted together.

90
00:05:59,437 --> 00:06:05,304
Selecting the correct environment is important because the
application depends on packages

91
00:06:05,304 --> 00:06:08,726
for numerical processing, images and checkpoint loading.

92
00:06:08,946 --> 00:06:12,504
Running the inference demonstration should not start training.

93
00:06:12,724 --> 00:06:18,385
The existing checkpoints are reused, and missing local assets
are reported explicitly

94
00:06:18,385 --> 00:06:21,216
rather than replaced by fabricated examples.

95
00:06:21,436 --> 00:06:26,139
Before showing predictions, the notebook displays the checkpoint
status.

96
00:06:26,359 --> 00:06:30,662
The application has eight main sensor routes and eight main
image routes,

97
00:06:30,662 --> 00:06:34,248
plus the additional Aalto gear sensor route for Motor Grader.

98
00:06:34,468 --> 00:06:38,494
A checkpoint can be present on disk without being trusted, and a

99
00:06:38,494 --> 00:06:42,520
trusted filename alone does not prove that a real prediction
will work.

100
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:45,977
The status table is therefore only the first check.

101
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:49,037
It is followed by actual inference calls.

102
00:06:49,257 --> 00:06:54,537
The local verification found all required checkpoint files and
their registrations.

103
00:06:54,757 --> 00:06:58,863
The saved models remain unchanged during this video preparation.

104
00:06:59,083 --> 00:07:04,148
The code archive deliberately excludes their large binaries, so
someone running a

105
00:07:04,148 --> 00:07:09,212
fresh copy needs the documented local assets as well as the
Python

106
00:07:09,212 --> 00:07:09,634
dependencies.

107
00:07:09,854 --> 00:07:15,233
The sensor loading code examines known file structures rather
than accepting every

108
00:07:15,233 --> 00:07:17,026
numerical table as interchangeable.

109
00:07:17,246 --> 00:07:24,844
Supported CSV schemas identify expected channel names for
Ottawa, UODS, MCC5, JUST

110
00:07:24,844 --> 00:07:26,743
and Aalto sources.

111
00:07:26,963 --> 00:07:31,950
Original MAT recordings are also supported for relevant bearing
sources.

112
00:07:32,170 --> 00:07:36,671
CORA recordings have a source-specific naming and acquisition
convention.

113
00:07:36,891 --> 00:07:42,251
These checks matter because sampling rates, channel meanings and
units affect the

114
00:07:42,251 --> 00:07:43,145
extracted features.

115
00:07:43,365 --> 00:07:48,515
A pressure column cannot be substituted for an acceleration
channel merely because

116
00:07:48,515 --> 00:07:49,803
both contain numbers.

117
00:07:50,023 --> 00:07:55,583
The application rejects an unrecognized CSV schema instead of
passing incompatible values

118
00:07:55,583 --> 00:07:56,974
into a model.

119
00:07:57,194 --> 00:08:03,693
Source recognition is not a universal machine-identification
algorithm; it identifies compatibility with

120
00:08:03,693 --> 00:08:08,026
the laboratory pipelines already implemented in this project.

121
00:08:08,246 --> 00:08:13,365
Cleaning in this project means validating the measurements and
applying the source-specific

122
00:08:13,365 --> 00:08:15,498
preparation expected by a model.

123
00:08:15,718 --> 00:08:20,366
Readers check numeric values and whether enough samples are
available for a

124
00:08:20,366 --> 00:08:21,528
complete feature window.

125
00:08:21,748 --> 00:08:26,596
Later checks reject nonfinite features and feature sets that do
not match

126
00:08:26,596 --> 00:08:27,404
the checkpoint.

127
00:08:27,624 --> 00:08:31,651
These controls prevent a model from receiving the wrong columns
in the

128
00:08:31,651 --> 00:08:32,322
wrong order.

129
00:08:32,542 --> 00:08:38,951
Sensor features include quantities such as root mean square,
standard deviation, crest

130
00:08:38,951 --> 00:08:41,622
factor and selected frequency-domain summaries.

131
00:08:41,842 --> 00:08:46,544
Some sources use shaft-order information when rotational speed
is available.

132
00:08:46,764 --> 00:08:51,046
Preprocessing is not simply deleting missing rows and hoping for
a good

133
00:08:51,046 --> 00:08:51,403
score.

134
00:08:51,623 --> 00:08:56,098
Its purpose is to preserve a consistent relationship between the
original measurement,

135
00:08:56,098 --> 00:09:00,199
the extracted features and the model that was trained on them.

136
00:09:00,419 --> 00:09:04,421
Root mean square is the square root of the average squared
signal

137
00:09:04,421 --> 00:09:04,755
amplitude.

138
00:09:04,975 --> 00:09:10,543
It summarizes signal energy but does not independently identify
a particular fault.

139
00:09:10,763 --> 00:09:15,325
Crest factor compares a peak amplitude with the root mean square
value

140
00:09:15,325 --> 00:09:17,225
and can describe impulsive behaviour.

141
00:09:17,445 --> 00:09:22,136
Spectral features summarize the distribution of energy across
frequency.

142
00:09:22,356 --> 00:09:28,043
In sources where speed is known, shaft-order features express
frequency relative to

143
00:09:28,043 --> 00:09:28,517
rotation.

144
00:09:28,737 --> 00:09:33,743
These measurements can change with operating conditions as well
as damage, which

145
00:09:33,743 --> 00:09:37,080
explains why speed and load separation are important.

146
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:41,349
The model learns combinations of features from labelled
examples.

147
00:09:41,569 --> 00:09:45,384
A large feature value is not automatically a failure warning.

148
00:09:45,604 --> 00:09:51,195
At inference, the selected checkpoint determines exactly which
feature columns are required

149
00:09:51,195 --> 00:09:54,457
and which preprocessing pipeline must be applied.

150
00:09:54,677 --> 00:09:59,434
The main evaluation safeguards are visible in the notebook split
demonstration.

151
00:09:59,654 --> 00:10:03,922
Complete recordings or operating groups are assigned to the test
side.

152
00:10:04,142 --> 00:10:08,515
Individual windows from a held-out recording cannot be placed in
training.

153
00:10:08,735 --> 00:10:13,874
Pump uses separate speed profiles or operating speeds for its
two datasets.

154
00:10:14,094 --> 00:10:16,435
CORA holds out whole speed settings.

155
00:10:16,655 --> 00:10:20,991
Haul Truck sensor evaluation uses held-out bearing identities.

156
00:10:21,211 --> 00:10:26,173
The aligned Motor Grader sensor experiment leaves gear pairs
out, while its

157
00:10:26,173 --> 00:10:28,241
photo task uses source groups.

158
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:33,784
These protocols are not identical, and their differences remain
part of the

159
00:10:33,784 --> 00:10:34,227
interpretation.

160
00:10:34,447 --> 00:10:39,017
Inner validation selects models or training settings within the
training data.

161
00:10:39,237 --> 00:10:45,392
This reduces direct leakage from the final evaluation group,
although dataset confounding

162
00:10:45,392 --> 00:10:50,007
and limited independent specimens can still restrict scientific
conclusions.

163
00:10:50,227 --> 00:10:55,641
The sensor code defines several candidate classifiers rather
than forcing a single

164
00:10:55,641 --> 00:10:57,446
algorithm onto every dataset.

165
00:10:57,666 --> 00:11:04,205
The candidate family includes random forest, extra trees,
histogram gradient boosting, a

166
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:08,019
radial-basis support vector machine and logistic regression.

167
00:11:08,239 --> 00:11:13,559
Scaling is contained inside the relevant estimator pipeline, so
its parameters are

168
00:11:13,559 --> 00:11:15,333
fitted with training data.

169
00:11:15,553 --> 00:11:18,067
Class weighting is used where configured.

170
00:11:18,287 --> 00:11:24,124
The chosen candidate can differ across evaluation folds and
across application mappings.

171
00:11:24,344 --> 00:11:29,705
The notebook displays these settings by instantiating the
candidate factories and reading

172
00:11:29,705 --> 00:11:30,599
their parameters.

173
00:11:30,819 --> 00:11:35,570
Deployment uses the saved final estimator and its selected
feature list.

174
00:11:35,790 --> 00:11:40,073
It does not repeat candidate selection each time a user uploads
a

175
00:11:40,073 --> 00:11:40,430
file.

176
00:11:40,650 --> 00:11:46,200
This keeps inference reproducible and avoids confusing
prediction latency with a new

177
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,125
training experiment.

178
00:11:47,345 --> 00:11:52,226
The visual route reads a supported image, applies its configured
transforms and

179
00:11:52,226 --> 00:11:55,074
uses a saved model to obtain probabilities.

180
00:11:55,294 --> 00:11:59,555
Seven main image routes use ResNet18-based classifiers.

181
00:11:59,775 --> 00:12:06,492
Motor Grader tooth photographs follow a separate path: frozen
ResNet18 features feed

182
00:12:06,492 --> 00:12:08,171
a logistic-regression classifier.

183
00:12:08,391 --> 00:12:12,834
This distinction is important when explaining which model
produced an answer.

184
00:12:13,054 --> 00:12:18,077
Inference runs without gradient calculation and with the model
in evaluation mode.

185
00:12:18,297 --> 00:12:23,019
The system is not trained to diagnose arbitrary whole-machine
photographs.

186
00:12:23,239 --> 00:12:28,763
Supported event frames, thermal frames, synthetic gear renders
and tooth crops have

187
00:12:28,763 --> 00:12:31,065
different visual meanings and provenance.

188
00:12:31,285 --> 00:12:35,229
A photo of an entire grader does not provide the same evidence

189
00:12:35,229 --> 00:12:37,201
as a labelled tooth inspection crop.

190
00:12:37,421 --> 00:12:41,258
Unknown image sources must remain unsupported or ambiguous.

191
00:12:41,478 --> 00:12:46,318
The central prediction function is the connection between the
notebook, command line

192
00:12:46,318 --> 00:12:47,931
and local upload page.

193
00:12:48,151 --> 00:12:52,991
It first handles the special tooth-image route when Motor Grader
is explicitly

194
00:12:52,991 --> 00:12:53,394
selected.

195
00:12:53,614 --> 00:12:56,848
Other inputs are passed through source identification.

196
00:12:57,068 --> 00:13:01,421
If a user selects a mapping incompatible with that source, the
function

197
00:13:01,421 --> 00:13:02,509
raises an error.

198
00:13:02,729 --> 00:13:07,397
If the source matches several candidates and no reliable choice
has been

199
00:13:07,397 --> 00:13:10,120
made, it returns an ambiguous equipment result.

200
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:15,568
Otherwise it scores the appropriate checkpoint, selects the most
probable class and

201
00:13:15,568 --> 00:13:17,310
assembles the answer fields.

202
00:13:17,530 --> 00:13:23,051
The common entry point reduces the risk that different
interfaces accidentally apply

203
00:13:23,051 --> 00:13:23,971
different preprocessing.

204
00:13:24,191 --> 00:13:29,942
It also keeps source identification separate from fault
classification, which is essential

205
00:13:29,942 --> 00:13:33,777
for equipment mappings that share one laboratory dataset.

206
00:13:33,997 --> 00:13:39,038
The notebook upload interface uses a file-upload widget, a
mapping dropdown and

207
00:13:39,038 --> 00:13:40,298
a prediction button.

208
00:13:40,518 --> 00:13:46,342
The upload accepts supported sensor recordings or image formats,
but format acceptance

209
00:13:46,342 --> 00:13:48,769
does not guarantee source compatibility.

210
00:13:48,989 --> 00:13:52,887
The callback first checks whether a file was actually supplied.

211
00:13:53,107 --> 00:13:58,049
It then passes the temporary input to the same application
prediction function.

212
00:13:58,269 --> 00:14:02,461
Automatic routing is useful only where the source can be
established.

213
00:14:02,681 --> 00:14:08,341
The dropdown remains necessary for shared laboratory formats and
the explicit gear-tooth

214
00:14:08,341 --> 00:14:09,284
inspection route.

215
00:14:09,504 --> 00:14:13,640
The interface should display either a condition prediction with
its model information

216
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:17,430
or a clear explanation of why the input cannot be scored.

217
00:14:17,650 --> 00:14:22,656
A user confirmation selects an application mapping; it does not
turn laboratory

218
00:14:22,656 --> 00:14:25,993
data into real measurements from that mining machine.

219
00:14:26,213 --> 00:14:30,717
This panel shows the actual output of a Pump sensor inference
call

220
00:14:30,717 --> 00:14:32,594
using an available local recording.

221
00:14:32,814 --> 00:14:38,735
The application identifies a compatible bearing source, extracts
the expected features and

222
00:14:38,735 --> 00:14:41,202
loads the trusted sensor checkpoint.

223
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:45,332
The predicted class and probability are returned with the model
name.

224
00:14:45,552 --> 00:14:49,942
The example is useful for demonstrating that the complete path
works from

225
00:14:49,942 --> 00:14:51,040
file to answer.

226
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:55,308
It must not be described as a fresh held-out accuracy
measurement.

227
00:14:55,528 --> 00:15:00,367
The route-check samples can be fitting data, and the archived
evaluation uses

228
00:15:00,367 --> 00:15:01,980
its own group separation.

229
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:07,264
The application mapping is Pump, while the source remains an
Ottawa bearing-rig

230
00:15:07,264 --> 00:15:07,685
measurement.

231
00:15:07,905 --> 00:15:13,082
That distinction keeps the demonstration truthful without
reducing the value of showing

232
00:15:13,082 --> 00:15:15,239
a real model execute successfully.

233
00:15:15,459 --> 00:15:20,437
The Pump image example uses a local event-camera frame with
known provenance.

234
00:15:20,657 --> 00:15:25,507
The model returns its current-condition classification and class
probabilities.

235
00:15:25,727 --> 00:15:30,560
An event frame represents changes observed by a dynamic-vision
sensor; it is

236
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:34,185
different from a standard RGB photograph of a pump.

237
00:15:34,405 --> 00:15:39,390
Its supported size and channel pattern help identify the source
family, while

238
00:15:39,390 --> 00:15:42,714
local source indexing can establish a unique mapping.

239
00:15:42,934 --> 00:15:48,524
The sensor and image examples are separate observations, not
synchronized recordings of

240
00:15:48,524 --> 00:15:49,456
one machine.

241
00:15:49,676 --> 00:15:54,292
Showing them beside each other demonstrates two independent
prediction routes.

242
00:15:54,512 --> 00:15:59,653
It does not demonstrate fusion, causal superiority of one
modality, or the

243
00:15:59,653 --> 00:16:04,365
ability to detect an internal bearing fault from an arbitrary
photograph.

244
00:16:04,585 --> 00:16:08,354
Those stronger claims would require additional matched evidence.

245
00:16:08,574 --> 00:16:13,708
Motor Grader needs special explanation because two component
tasks are retained.

246
00:16:13,928 --> 00:16:17,824
The original sensor route diagnoses slewing-bearing conditions.

247
00:16:18,044 --> 00:16:23,215
The aligned comparison adds an Aalto gear sensor checkpoint for
a broad

248
00:16:23,215 --> 00:16:24,508
healthy-versus-damaged gear target.

249
00:16:24,728 --> 00:16:29,299
Here the actual local Aalto recording produces a healthy
prediction with a

250
00:16:29,299 --> 00:16:31,965
probability of zero point nine eight seven.

251
00:16:32,185 --> 00:16:35,432
This is a deployment response on a fitting recording.

252
00:16:35,652 --> 00:16:39,502
It is not ninety-eight point seven percent held-out accuracy.

253
00:16:39,722 --> 00:16:44,920
The independent gear-pair experiment is the evidence used to
discuss generalization.

254
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:49,829
The Aalto dataset is a laboratory gearbox analogue, not a field
recording

255
00:16:49,829 --> 00:16:51,392
from a Motor Grader.

256
00:16:51,612 --> 00:16:57,329
Preserving both routes avoids deleting working evidence while
making the component comparison

257
00:16:57,329 --> 00:16:58,759
more mechanically defensible.

258
00:16:58,979 --> 00:17:03,801
The Motor Grader image route scores a real tooth inspection crop
using

259
00:17:03,801 --> 00:17:05,408
the saved feature-based classifier.

260
00:17:05,628 --> 00:17:10,835
The example panel shows the actual damaged-tooth prediction and
the fields returned

261
00:17:10,835 --> 00:17:12,137
by that implementation.

262
00:17:12,357 --> 00:17:16,967
The model confidence display is still an uncalibrated output and
should not

263
00:17:16,967 --> 00:17:20,040
be interpreted as certainty of real equipment failure.

264
00:17:20,260 --> 00:17:24,172
Sensor and image tasks share a broad gear-condition target, but
one label

265
00:17:24,172 --> 00:17:28,084
is attached to a gear-pair run and the other to a local

266
00:17:28,084 --> 00:17:28,736
tooth crop.

267
00:17:28,956 --> 00:17:30,914
Their physical gears are different.

268
00:17:31,134 --> 00:17:37,087
The existing tests therefore support a comparison of related
classification tasks, not

269
00:17:37,087 --> 00:17:39,071
a paired same-grader experiment.

270
00:17:39,291 --> 00:17:44,800
The original bearing checkpoint remains available independently
and should not be substituted

271
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:46,637
into this gear-tooth comparison.

272
00:17:46,857 --> 00:17:52,553
This execution supplies a compatible CORA recording without
selecting an equipment mapping.

273
00:17:52,773 --> 00:17:58,447
The expected behaviour is an ambiguous equipment response
listing the supported candidates.

274
00:17:58,667 --> 00:18:03,484
The system cannot infer that an identical laboratory source must
belong to

275
00:18:03,484 --> 00:18:05,491
one particular whole mining machine.

276
00:18:05,711 --> 00:18:10,117
This is a reliability feature, not a missing classification
trick that should

277
00:18:10,117 --> 00:18:11,953
be bypassed with a guess.

278
00:18:12,173 --> 00:18:16,930
Manual mapping confirmation allows a known task to be evaluated,
but it

279
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:20,894
does not create new evidence about the original physical
machine.

280
00:18:21,114 --> 00:18:24,211
The same principle applies to image provenance.

281
00:18:24,431 --> 00:18:29,025
A visually similar frame can remain ambiguous when its source
index cannot

282
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:30,556
establish a unique route.

283
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:36,565
The final demonstration should explain this behaviour clearly
rather than presenting every

284
00:18:36,565 --> 00:18:38,494
upload as automatic identification.

285
00:18:38,714 --> 00:18:45,128
The invalid-input examples test ordinary text, an unrecognized
CSV and corrupted image

286
00:18:45,128 --> 00:18:45,662
bytes.

287
00:18:45,882 --> 00:18:51,043
Each example was actually sent to the prediction function, and
the displayed

288
00:18:51,043 --> 00:18:53,193
response records the resulting rejection.

289
00:18:53,413 --> 00:18:57,745
These checks matter because an upload control can accept a
filename even

290
00:18:57,745 --> 00:18:59,551
when the content is unusable.

291
00:18:59,771 --> 00:19:04,655
The model-loading path also verifies checkpoint trust and
expected metadata.

292
00:19:04,875 --> 00:19:09,527
A missing or untrusted checkpoint must not be replaced with a
random

293
00:19:09,527 --> 00:19:11,465
estimator or a fabricated prediction.

294
00:19:11,685 --> 00:19:16,183
Errors should explain why the input could not be scored, while
leaving

295
00:19:16,183 --> 00:19:17,682
the working application stable.

296
00:19:17,902 --> 00:19:23,181
These examples demonstrate handling of specific tested cases;
they are not a

297
00:19:23,181 --> 00:19:27,140
guarantee that every imaginable malformed file has been
exhausted.

298
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:32,760
The complete route check executed thirty-nine saved-model
examples successfully, covering all eight

299
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:37,260
sensor and image mappings plus the additional Aalto gear route.

300
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:42,304
Unsupported-file rejection and shared-CORA ambiguity checks also
passed.

301
00:19:42,524 --> 00:19:47,676
The important qualification is the definition of pass: a model
loaded, accepted

302
00:19:47,676 --> 00:19:51,110
a compatible input and returned the required output.

303
00:19:51,330 --> 00:19:55,058
Two Drill Rig images were classified as healthy when their
source labels

304
00:19:55,058 --> 00:19:56,922
were gear wear and gear pitting.

305
00:19:57,142 --> 00:20:02,142
Those cases remain visible as prediction errors even though
execution succeeded.

306
00:20:02,362 --> 00:20:08,403
Earlier project verification recorded two hundred fifty-seven
local automated tests and a

307
00:20:08,403 --> 00:20:12,431
successful hosted workflow with two expected local-data skips.

308
00:20:12,651 --> 00:20:17,934
Those are historical verification records, not claims that the
entire test suite

309
00:20:17,934 --> 00:20:20,576
was rerun during this video preparation.

310
00:20:20,796 --> 00:20:25,101
The final report contains the independent experimental results.

311
00:20:25,321 --> 00:20:30,872
Pump reached ninety-five point eight three percent sensor
balanced accuracy and one

312
00:20:30,872 --> 00:20:35,498
hundred percent visual balanced accuracy under their respective
recording protocols.

313
00:20:35,718 --> 00:20:40,329
Those protocols and rigs differ, so the result does not
establish that

314
00:20:40,329 --> 00:20:41,866
vision is universally better.

315
00:20:42,086 --> 00:20:45,717
The CORA tasks showed weak transfer to unseen speeds.

316
00:20:45,937 --> 00:20:51,050
Haul Truck had weaker visual recognition and a load-confounded
ball-fault class.

317
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:56,455
Motor Grader's aligned gear sensor result was seventy-seven
point seven eight percent

318
00:20:56,455 --> 00:21:01,640
balanced accuracy, while the tooth-photo result was eighty-two
point five nine percent.

319
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:06,881
Its high raw photo accuracy is affected by class imbalance, and
damaged-tooth

320
00:21:06,881 --> 00:21:08,137
recall is lower.

321
00:21:08,357 --> 00:21:14,013
The poster uses qualitative findings, while the report preserves
the full numerical

322
00:21:14,013 --> 00:21:14,484
evidence.

323
00:21:14,704 --> 00:21:19,352
Secondary time-split experiments use the first sixty percent of
a recording for

324
00:21:19,352 --> 00:21:24,000
training, discard a ten percent gap and test on the last thirty

325
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:24,387
percent.

326
00:21:24,607 --> 00:21:28,764
Several saved results are much higher than the unseen-speed
results.

327
00:21:28,984 --> 00:21:32,835
This is not a reason to hide the more difficult evaluations.

328
00:21:33,055 --> 00:21:35,838
The two protocols ask different questions.

329
00:21:36,058 --> 00:21:40,684
A later segment of a known recording can retain the same speed,

330
00:21:40,684 --> 00:21:42,996
specimen and acquisition signature as training.

331
00:21:43,216 --> 00:21:47,761
A gap reduces direct temporal overlap, but it does not create a

332
00:21:47,761 --> 00:21:49,655
new machine or operating condition.

333
00:21:49,875 --> 00:21:54,078
The report labels these scores separately and notes that fitting
settings and

334
00:21:54,078 --> 00:21:55,479
sample pools can differ.

335
00:21:55,699 --> 00:22:00,754
No score from this procedure establishes future failure
forecasting, and no unsupported

336
00:22:00,754 --> 00:22:05,387
time-split result is assigned to a mapping without a saved
experiment.

337
00:22:05,607 --> 00:22:11,419
The practical outcome is a working educational prototype for
component inspection and

338
00:22:11,419 --> 00:22:12,872
reproducible model comparison.

339
00:22:13,092 --> 00:22:19,660
It demonstrates data ingestion, feature preparation, trusted
model reuse, ambiguity handling and

340
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:22,944
prediction output through a common interface.

341
00:22:23,164 --> 00:22:27,479
Its remaining limitations are scientific as well as operational.

342
00:22:27,699 --> 00:22:33,932
Some datasets share records, image crops remain related,
synthetic renders need validation

343
00:22:33,932 --> 00:22:39,646
against real photographs, and confidence values are not
calibrated failure risks.

344
00:22:39,866 --> 00:22:44,382
The code package also needs local data and checkpoints to run
the

345
00:22:44,382 --> 00:22:45,134
full demonstration.

346
00:22:45,354 --> 00:22:50,982
Before a real maintenance decision could rely on this system,
additional work

347
00:22:50,982 --> 00:22:56,610
would need site-specific measurements, balanced operating
conditions, independent machines and a clear

348
00:22:56,610 --> 00:22:58,486
assessment of missed-fault costs.

349
00:22:58,706 --> 00:23:05,209
The present software should support investigation and
explanation, not replace qualified engineering

350
00:23:05,209 --> 00:23:05,750
judgment.

351
00:23:05,970 --> 00:23:11,596
To conclude, the coding phase provides one integrated notebook
backed by a

352
00:23:11,596 --> 00:23:13,003
reusable Python implementation.

353
00:23:13,223 --> 00:23:18,582
It accepts supported sensor recordings or component images,
checks source compatibility, loads

354
00:23:18,582 --> 00:23:23,941
an existing model and returns a fault label with model
information and

355
00:23:23,941 --> 00:23:24,387
probability.

356
00:23:24,607 --> 00:23:30,379
Where source evidence cannot distinguish equipment mappings, the
system reports ambiguity rather

357
00:23:30,379 --> 00:23:31,341
than guessing.

358
00:23:31,561 --> 00:23:36,592
Real local execution checks confirm that the supported routes
run, including the

359
00:23:36,592 --> 00:23:40,366
aligned Aalto gear sensor and Motor Grader tooth-image paths.

360
00:23:40,586 --> 00:23:46,401
The final report explains the actual held-out results, the
separate time-split experiments

361
00:23:46,401 --> 00:23:48,339
and the unsuccessful cases.

362
00:23:48,559 --> 00:23:54,337
The project is complete as a laboratory-based demonstration with
scientific limitations.

363
00:23:54,557 --> 00:24:00,470
Future work should improve independent data and validation
before expanding claims about

364
00:24:00,470 --> 00:24:03,426
mining-field reliability or future failure prediction.

365
00:24:03,646 --> 00:24:05,097
Thank you for watching.
